#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:1
msgid "Source Installation on Ubuntu"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:3
msgid "These instructions apply to Ubuntu Focal (20.04) and Jammy (22.04)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:5
msgid "Install tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:7
msgid ""
"The use of some additional tools is recommended to help with the source "
"compilation, although other ways of correctly getting and building the "
"sources are also possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:10
msgid ""
"The easiest way to get the sources of all libraries is to use [vcstool]"
"(https://github.com/dirk-thomas/vcstool)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:13
msgid ""
"To compile all the different libraries and gz-sim in the right order [colcon]"
"(https://colcon.readthedocs.io/en/released/) is recommended. The colcon tool "
"is available on all platforms using pip (or pip3, if pip fails)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:17
msgid ""
"Some tools require Python 3.5 (or higher) which is not the default option on "
"some platforms (like Ubuntu Focal). The Python [virtualenv](https://"
"virtualenv.pypa.io/en/latest/) could be a useful solution in cases where the "
"default option cannot be easily changed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:22
msgid "Generic tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:24
msgid "Install tools needed by this tutorial:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:26
msgid "sudo apt install python3-pip lsb-release gnupg curl git\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:30
msgid "vcstool and colcon from pip"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:32
msgid "PIP is available on all platforms:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:34
msgid "pip install vcstool || pip3 install vcstool\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:38
msgid ""
"pip install -U colcon-common-extensions || pip3 install -U colcon-common-"
"extensions\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:42
msgid ""
"Check that no errors were printed while installing with PIP. If your system "
"is not recognising the commands, and you're using a system that is "
"compatible with Debian or Ubuntu packages, see the instructions below to "
"install using `apt`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:44
msgid ""
"After installing `vcstool` and `colcon` with PIP, you may need to add their "
"executables to your `$PATH`. Check where the installation of these packages "
"took place:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:47
msgid ""
"pip show vcstool || pip3 show vcstool | grep Location\n"
"\n"
"pip show colcon-common-extensions || pip3 show colcon-common-extensions | "
"grep Location\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:53
msgid ""
"If your install path is prefixed with `$HOME/.local`, you'll probably need "
"to add the executables within this directory to your `$PATH` in order to "
"avoid \"command not found\" errors when using `vcstool` and `colcon` later "
"on:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:55
msgid "export PATH=$PATH:$HOME/.local/bin/\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:59
msgid "vcstool and colcon from apt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:61
msgid ""
"An alternative method is to use the `.deb` packages available on Debian or "
"Ubuntu:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:63
msgid ""
"sudo sh -c 'echo \"deb http://packages.ros.org/ros2/ubuntu $(lsb_release -"
"sc) main\" > /etc/apt/sources.list.d/ros2-latest.list'\n"
"curl -s https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ros/rosdistro/master/ros.asc | "
"sudo apt-key add -\n"
"sudo apt-get update\n"
"sudo apt-get install python3-vcstool python3-colcon-common-extensions\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:70
msgid "Getting the sources"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:72
msgid ""
"The instructions below use some UNIX commands to manage directories but the "
"equivalent alternatives on Windows should provide the same result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:75
msgid ""
"The first step is to create a developer workspace in which `vcstool` and "
"`colcon` can work:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:78
msgid ""
"mkdir -p ~/workspace/src\n"
"cd ~/workspace/\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:83
msgid ""
"Use `vcstool` to automatically retrieve all the Gazebo libraries sources "
"from their repositories:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:86
msgid ""
"vcs import --input https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gazebo-tooling/"
"gazebodistro/master/collection-garden.yaml src\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:90
msgid "The src subdirectory should contain all the sources ready to be built."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:92
msgid "Install dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:94
msgid ""
"Before compiling it is necessary to install all the dependencies of the "
"different packages that compose the Garden collection. Every platform has a "
"different method to install software dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:98
msgid "Add `packages.osrfoundation.org` to the apt sources list:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:100
msgid ""
"sudo curl https://packages.osrfoundation.org/gazebo.gpg --output /usr/share/"
"keyrings/pkgs-osrf-archive-keyring.gpg\n"
"echo \"deb [arch=$(dpkg --print-architecture) signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/"
"pkgs-osrf-archive-keyring.gpg] http://packages.osrfoundation.org/gazebo/"
"ubuntu-stable $(lsb_release -cs) main\" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/"
"gazebo-stable.list > /dev/null\n"
"sudo apt-get update\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:106
msgid ""
"The command below must be run from a workspace with the Gazebo source code "
"and will install all dependencies in Ubuntu:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:108
msgid ""
"cd ~/workspace/src\n"
"sudo apt -y install \\\n"
"  $(sort -u $(find . -iname 'packages-'`lsb_release -cs`'.apt' -o -iname "
"'packages.apt' | grep -v '/\\.git/') | sed '/gz\\|sdf/d' | tr '\\n' ' ')\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:114
msgid "Building the Gazebo Libraries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:116
msgid ""
"Once the compiler and all the sources are in place it is time to compile "
"them. Start the procedure by changing into the workspace and listing the "
"packages recognized by `colcon`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:120
msgid ""
"cd ~/workspace/\n"
"colcon graph\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:125
msgid ""
"`colcon graph` should list the Gazebo libraries with an [interdependency "
"diagram](https://colcon.readthedocs.io/en/released/reference/verb/graph."
"html#example-output). If that is the case, then you are ready to build the "
"whole set of libraries:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:130
msgid "colcon build --merge-install\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:134
msgid "To speed up the build process, you could also disable tests by using"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:136
msgid "colcon build --cmake-args -DBUILD_TESTING=OFF --merge-install\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:140
msgid ""
"To use debuggers activate debug symbols. Gazebo will run slower, but you'll "
"be able to use GDB:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:142
msgid ""
"colcon build --cmake-args ' -DBUILD_TESTING=OFF' ' -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug' "
"--merge-install\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:146
msgid "To build a specific package with all its dependent packages:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:148
msgid "colcon build --merge-install --packages-up-to PACKAGE_NAME\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:152
msgid "To build a single package:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:154
msgid "colcon build --packages-select PACKAGE_NAME\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:158
msgid ""
"Visit [colcon documentation](https://colcon.readthedocs.io/en/released/#) to "
"view more `colcon` build and test options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:160
msgid ""
"If there are no errors, all the binaries should be ready to use. You can "
"check the [Troubleshooting](troubleshooting.md#ubuntu) section for errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:162
msgid "Using the workspace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:164
msgid "The workspace needs to be sourced every time a new terminal is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:166
msgid "Run the following command to source the workspace in bash:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:168
msgid ". ~/workspace/install/setup.bash\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:172
msgid "Or in zsh:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:174
msgid ". ~/workspace/install/setup.zsh\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:178
msgid ""
"This is the end of the source install instructions; head back to the "
"[Getting started](getstarted) page to start using Gazebo!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:181
msgid "Uninstalling source-based install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:183
msgid ""
"A source-based install can be \"uninstalled\" using several methods, "
"depending on the results you want:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:186
msgid ""
"If you installed your workspace with `colcon` as instructed above, "
"\"uninstalling\" could be just a matter of opening a new terminal and not "
"sourcing the workspace's `setup.sh`. This way, your environment will behave "
"as though Gazebo is not installed on your system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:191
msgid ""
"If, in addition to not wanting to use the libraries, you're also trying to "
"free up space, you can delete the entire workspace directory with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:194
msgid "rm -rf ~/workspace\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:198
msgid ""
"If you want to keep the source code, you can remove the `install` / "
"`build` / `log` directories as desired, leaving the `src` directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:201
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:203
msgid "See [Troubleshooting](troubleshooting.md#ubuntu)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:205
msgid "QML Debugging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:207
msgid "To perform QML debugging you'll need:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:209
msgid "Add `--cmake-args -DDQT_QML_DEBUG` flag to colcon"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:210
msgid "QtCreator"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:212
msgid "You will need to build Gazebo with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:214
msgid "colcon build --cmake-args -DQT_QML_DEBUG --merge-install\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:218
msgid ""
"**Note:** Advanced users may note that only the `gz-sim` project needs this "
"flag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:220
msgid ""
"After that's done, launching `gz sim -g` will result in the following "
"message:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:222
msgid ""
"QML debugging is enabled. Only use this in a safe environment.\n"
"QML Debugger: Waiting for connection on port 40000...\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:227
msgid ""
"After that you can just head to `QtCreator -> Debug -> Start Debugging -> "
"Attach to QML Port...` and enter the QML port"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:231
msgid "![](images/GzGuiQmlDebugging01.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:233
msgid "Once you click there, set the port number to 40000 and hit ok"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:235
msgid "![](images/GzGuiQmlDebugging02.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:237
msgid ""
"We're working to improve QtCreator integration so that it works out of the "
"box."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:239
msgid ""
"The ruby `gz` script doesn't yet pass the necessary command line arguments "
"to the application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:241
msgid ""
"Note that because all instances will try to use port 40000, only one "
"instance can use it. If you shutdown the process and restart it immediately "
"too quickly, the OS may still claim the port is in use and hence the 2nd "
"(re)launch will not listen to QML debugger attach requests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:246
msgid "Avoid QML stall waiting for debugger on startup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:248
msgid ""
"During development, you may find troublesome that `gz sim -g` won't actually "
"start until QtCreator hooks to the QML Debugging port."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:251
msgid ""
"If that's a problem, you can edit the C++ file `gz-sim/src/gz.cc` and remove "
"`block` from it. E.g."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:254
msgid ""
"// The following:\n"
"const_cast<char *>(\n"
"      \"-qmljsdebugger=port:40000,block,services:DebugMessages,QmlDebugger,"
"\"\n"
"      \"V8Debugger,QmlInspector,DebugTranslation\")\n"
"\n"
"// Must become the following\n"
"const_cast<char *>(\n"
"      \"-qmljsdebugger=port:40000,services:DebugMessages,QmlDebugger,\"\n"
"      \"V8Debugger,QmlInspector,DebugTranslation\")\n"
msgstr ""
